    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455-a1">

                <pb facs="0884" n="760" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg760"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 124.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Crosby to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >War Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1881-04-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 19,
                    1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information copy of a dispatch from the commanding officer, district of New
                    Mexico, dated the 9th instant, reporting Mexican troops operating against
                    hostile Indians, and that there are 370 regular Mexican troops at El Paso,
                    Mexico; also, that he has ordered Indian companies and detachments with cavalry
                    to the Mexican line to co-operate if Indians are driven north.</p>
                <p>A similar copy is furnished this day to the honorable Secretary of the
                    Interior.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>H. T. CROSBY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chief Clerk,<lb/>For the
                            Secretary of War in his absence.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
